  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a weighted simple undirected graph with NNN vertices, which are numbered from 111 to NNN. You are guaranteed that vertex 111 is not an articulation point (which means that even after removing the vertex 111, the remaining graph is connected) and has an edge connecting it to each of the other N−1N-1N−1 vertices.\n\nFor each K∈{1,2,…,N−1}K \\in \\{1, 2, \\ldots, N-1\\}K∈{1,2,…,N−1} you need to find the minimum weight of a spanning tree where the degree of vertex 111 is equal to KKK.\n\n###Input:\n\n\nThe first line of input contains two integers N,MN, MN,M: the number of vertices and edges in the graph.\nEach of the next MMM lines contains three integers Ui,Vi,WiU_i, V_i, W_iUi​,Vi​,Wi​, denoting an edge between vertices UiU_iUi​ and ViV_iVi​ with weight WiW_iWi​.\n###Output:\nPrint N−1N-1N−1 integers in a single line -  the minimum weight of a spanning tree where the degree of vertex 111 is equal to 1,2,…,N−11, 2, \\ldots, N-11,2,…,N−1.\n\n###Constraints\n\n\n2≤N≤100 0002 \\leq N \\leq 100\\,0002≤N≤100000\n2N−3≤M≤200 0002N - 3 \\leq M \\leq 200\\,0002N−3≤M≤200000\n1≤Wi≤200 0001 \\leq W_i \\leq 200\\,0001≤Wi​≤200000\n1≤Ui&lt;Vi≤N1 \\leq U_i &lt; V_i \\leq N1≤Ui​&lt;Vi​≤N\nIt is guaranteed that the graph contains no multiple edges and vertex 111 is not an articulation point and its degree is equal to N−1N-1N−1.\n###Subtasks\n\n\n10 points : 2≤N≤52 \\leq N \\leq 52≤N≤5\n10 points : 2≤N≤5002 \\leq N \\leq 5002≤N≤500\n10 points : 2≤N≤10 0002 \\leq N \\leq 10\\,0002≤N≤10000\n70 points : 2≤N≤100 0002 \\leq N \\leq 100\\,0002≤N≤100000",
